WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.980
Ichigo...

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:03.640
Um?

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.320
This time let’s go to the beach.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.360
Eh?

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.410
The research facilities at Southern Cross
Marina also double as a chalet.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.480
I’m sure you’d be interested...

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.080
No... wait.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.530
You’ve always done your job well.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.540
Shirogane...

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.840
W-why has he invited me?

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.460
<i>I will... be your...</i>

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.800
Wuahh~!! It’s the sea, the sea, the sea...

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.560
It’s the sea!

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.480
What a beautiful beach this is.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.780
A chalet in a place like this,

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.000
Ryou never fails to surprise, does he?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.170
It’s everyone’s summer vacation, after all... I guess...

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.080
Something wrong?

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.470
Nah! Not at all.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.180
Here I go!

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.850
Here goes!

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.900
Waaah~! This feels good.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.030
I’m surfing too!

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.490
Hey, isn’t that Fujiwara Zakuro?!

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.280
You sure? You must be mistaken.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.570
Let’s take a closer look.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:47.460
It is!

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.090
Minto. Let’s swim.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.130
Oneesama!

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:12.020
What? Retasu didn’t swim?

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.650
Retasu-oneechan doesn’t want to swim?

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.570
Well, everyone had so much fun...

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.490
Now... what is Retasu’s power called again?

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.540
It’s “Sunameri” right?

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.700
Oh yes,

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.040
Living in Japan’s Seto Inland Sea and other areas, they’re a close relative to the dolphin,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.210
they bear live young, and display
cute looks and behaviour...

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.880
even their feeding habits bear little difference to dolphins.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.510
They’re really fascinating creatures.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.470
A cousin of the dolphin? Then why
doesn’t Retasu-oneechan swim?

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.050
Well, I really never swam before...

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:49.440
It has nothing to do with the Mew Mew powers at all.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:55.400
Speaking of such, becoming a cat
did not make me run after mice.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.400
iriomote yamaneko

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.060
How true.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.410
Even though I turned into a parakeet,
I’ve not sung karaoke yet.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.410
nodojiroruri-inko

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:05.330
Jyann~! Bu-Ling was already eating
meat before becoming a lion!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.580
golden lion tamarin

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.030
Attention:

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.580
the Golden Lion Tamarin belongs
to the monkey family. Nya~!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.300
Shall I eat you?

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.460
hai iro ookami

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.460
Even if you did, I’d taste terrible.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.090
But Retasu...

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.090
wouldn’t it be boring not being able to swim in the sea?

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.430
Absolutely not,

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:33.560
I love the sea. Enjoying the breeze
can be just as soothing.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.520
I see, I guess you’re right.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.150
Yeah, it really feels good!

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:46.040
Sigh... if only Aoyama-kun had come along...

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.910
Hey, isn’t that Ryou?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.460
Huh?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.460
Wow, he really knows how to surf!

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.710
There’s Akasaka-san too.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.750
Just look at them go.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.260
So cool!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:18.730
Look Pie! The oceans on Earth have
many fascinating life forms.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.860
Until proper research is done,
I suggest you leave them alone.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.230
It’s fine...

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.370
Iruka, why did you still come along if you can’t swim?

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.330
That’s what I’m here for.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.410
Bleh, you’re being willful.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:37.130
Having Iruka for a name and not being
able to swim is a bit strange isn’t it?

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.670
You there!!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:45.220
Stop that guys! To bully a lone girl
like her is just terrible!

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.220
Besides, we ladies like to know what happened...

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.260
Old hag!

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.270
Old hag!??

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.230
Old hag??

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.770
Those awful kids!

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.270
Relax Ichigo-san.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.740
Really terrible!

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.620
Are you alright?

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:06.820
Thanks.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.780
Unbelievable!
Kids are awful these days...

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.700
So you are getting old...

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.540
Can’t help feeling down because you can’t swim?

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.750
You’re called Iruka-chan?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.670
Yes.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.170
Alright, we will teach you how to swim!

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.680
That’s right, swim well and those
boys will have nothing to say.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:30.880
Why not?

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:32.800
You don’t have to be shy.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.650
But, even if I practice,
I still can’t swim.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.690
Don’t say that.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.770
We’ll show you how later...

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.650
No really I can’t... just can’t.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.290
Well, Iruka-chan, why don’t we learn swimming together?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.580
The truth is, I can’t swim either.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.620
I see... that may be a good idea.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.000
That way, the two of you can learn together.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:04.840
Iruka-chan?

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:11.510
It’s OK guys,
I’ll try to handle it from here.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.470
“Try”? Even though you don’t know how to swim?

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:20.470
True, I don’t... well,
have fun swimming everyone.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:22.110
Shall we go Iruka-chan?

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:27.030
Retasu... what will she do?

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:32.950
It’s not easy for someone who swims
to know how a non-swimmer feels.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.630
Iruka-chan, why don’t you swim?

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.420
I’m afraid of the water.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.800
I see... same as me perhaps.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:54.590
How about, we practice immersing our face in the water?

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:56.430
Eh? But...

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:00.890
Ready? This time I’ll go first.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.820
Take a very deep breath and...

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.570
Retasu-oneechan?

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:18.560
I’m fine, let’s try again.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.460
Take a deep breath...

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.230
I can’t see anything...

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:58.910
Entering the sea by a gentle slope is probably the best.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.620
I like the sea very much too.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.620
The fact is, I DO know how to swim.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.330
Eh? Is it true?

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:09.050
Then... what made you stop swimming?

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.880
Well... one day I was out gathering ark shells...

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.130
<i>A little more..</i>

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.310
<i>Yay!</i>

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.690
<i>Helppppp~!!</i>

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.890
...from then on,
I got scared of the water.

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.980
S-so thats what happened.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:33.820
But, I really love the sea,

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:38.150
just by covering my ears, I can hear the seagulls...

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:43.790
If I could swim again, I could go almost
anywhere, and do anything...

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.250
Iruka-chan...

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.960
I... want to swim once again...

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.000
once again...

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.510
I will swim too!

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.720
How are you going to do that?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.470
I don’t yet know for sure, but if I
try hard enough, it might just...

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.770
Don’t do it, you’ll drown!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.150
No, I’ll give it a shot.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:13.110
Perhaps if I can swim, Iruka-chan
will once again want to swim.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:14.150
But...

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:40.220
Oh no! Retasu-oneechan is drowning!!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.780
Umm?

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.570
What’s that?

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:04.200
<i>Retasu!</i>

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.800
<i>Retasu!?</i>

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.280
<i>Retasu!</i>

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:09.400
<i>Retasu-oneechan!</i>

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:11.750
<i>Retasu-oneechan!!</i>

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:18.630
You alright? Retasu, you alright?

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:24.930
Yay, Retasu-oneechan is alive!

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.220
Everyone... came to my rescue?

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:30.670
Thank you so much.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.680
What really happened?

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:34.940
Leaping into the water like that...

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:35.720
Well...

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:36.900
I’m sorry.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.740
Retasu-oneechan, I’m sorry!

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:47.660
Retasu-oneechan was doing her best
to help me when this happened.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:53.450
Iruka-chan, I’m really sorry to have caused you such worry.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:56.030
Nope... I appreciate it.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:58.240
Next time let’s pick a shallower spot.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.370
No, it’s fine.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:03.140
If it can’t be done, it can’t be done.

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:05.000
Iruka-chan...

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.720
I’ll go home now.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.820
Wowww, great!

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.280
IT’S DINNER TIME!

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:24.230
Café Mew Mew’s
special service — Hors D’oeuvre.

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:26.450
Itadakimasu!

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:30.780
This is delicious!

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.380
Well, feeling any better?

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:40.340
Sort of...

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.840
Is something bothering you?

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.800
I still can’t do it... can I?

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:53.830
Even now... I still lack the strength...

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:57.230
Retasu, you need to have more faith in yourself.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.430
Telling yourself that you can... meeting
every subsequent challenge.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:05.480
The truth about confidence is... just do your best.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:07.650
It’s a little too early to give up now.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.530
Faith?

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.010
Retasu, you want to play beach ball?

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.510
Thank you, but I’m not feeling so good.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.350
Well, join us when you feel better.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:31.760
Self-confidence... how do I get that..

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.880
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:33.810
Retasu-oneechan!

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:35.730
Iruka-chan.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.140
Alright, here we go!

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:40.690
Take that!

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.150
Here! Oneesama!

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:44.860
Here you go!

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.190
I’m sorry I went home yesterday...

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:50.650
It can’t be helped, since I can’t swim.

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:56.360
No, you did your best trying to give me confidence.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:57.660
I was really happy.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:58.540
Iruka-chan.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.160
After that l realized:

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.800
It’s not like I won’t ever swim again...

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:08.650
Though I’m afraid of water now,
someday I’ll overcome my fears.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.270
That’s how I feel.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.500
Eh?

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.810
I owe it all to Retasu-oneechan.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.270
I-Is that so?

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.730
I thought to myself,

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.280
“That was great. Retasu-oneechan will most certainly make a good swimmer”.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.810
Nice attack Minto.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:24.240
Nice, isn’t it, oneesama?

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:26.560
That’s... no way...

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.520
I’m sure you will.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:30.030
What makes you think so?

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:32.400
Someone who really can’t swim

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.980
...will never have the courage to leap into the water like you did.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.040
Like I said, the day will come when you’ll swim.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:38.790
Yes!

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.570
<i>We haven’t lost yet!</i>

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:41.700
<i>Let’s go!</i>

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.040
It’s time to move on.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.040
<i>Fight!!</i>

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:51.040
What’s happening?

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:52.430
The sea wasn’t like this...

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:00.480
It’s dangerous,
please get out of the water!

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:04.930
What’s with this wind...

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.220
Why now...

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.230
Ichigo! The Aliens are here.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:16.030
Pie! Tart!

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:18.710
What are you two doing here?

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.240
It’s none of your business.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:23.080
We’ll leave the sea the way it is.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.200
We also found some impressive monsters.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.680
Now check this out!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.090
Show yourselves, Chimera Animas!

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.590
What do you think? Scary aren’t they?

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:38.060
They’re from outer space.

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:39.410
What do you mean?

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.380
You only made them larger that’s all.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:43.510
Sea urchin monster?

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:43.510
What’s so magnificent about it?

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.570
Most likely, it’s gonna rain.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.280
Gahh! Why isn’t anyone scared?

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.270
Those creatures can be found anywhere in the sea.

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:53.730
In this case... let’s transform.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:55.940
Oh yeah, let’s go everyone!

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:57.270
Stay here OK?

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:58.660
Yes, Retasu-oneechan.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.660
Mew Mew Lettuce METAMORPHO-SE!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:22.020
Retasu-oneechan is part of Mew Mew?

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:26.390
Mew Mew Strawberry METAMORPHO-SE!

00:15:57.460 --> 00:16:01.520
Everyone’s having fun during summer,
it won’t be given over to weird incidents!

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:06.520
For the Earth’s future,
I’ll be of service! ~Nya!

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.610
Now we have become the agents of incidents?

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.490
Today is a big service. ATTACK!

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:19.150
Wait, what is this stuff?

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:19.790
Huh?

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:22.900
Let’s split into two groups!

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:23.790
This is...

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.670
(Starfish, charge!)

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.380
Look out!

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:31.340
(Electric shock attack!)

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.840
Geez, I’m getting a shock...

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:41.800
We must run!

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:46.310
There’s nowhere to run!!

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:48.590
That’s right, run, run!

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:52.100
Oh no! We’re surrounded.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.740
So do you want to call it a day?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.350
There seems to be no way out?

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:57.200
There’s no weakness at all.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.690
Anyone know?

00:16:58.690 --> 00:16:59.560
No.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.160
Nope.

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:04.250
Somebody help...

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.960
Help... anyone...

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.960
Oh no! Komura, Takeshi, Yousuke!

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:13.130
Oh no, someone fell into the water.
We’ve got to save them!

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:16.550
Ah, Iruka-chan?!

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.210
Komura!!!

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:19.550
Wait, that’s...

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:21.140
Mew Lettuce.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:22.520
(Stay down!)

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:27.220
Doesn’t she treasure her life?
Since she can’t swim will she be alright?

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:29.470
Don’t worry, she’ll succeed.

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:32.680
Putting others above oneself...

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.890
We’ll deal with these creatures here.

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:35.900
OK.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:41.660
<i>Iruka-chan!</i>

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.490
What is this... terrible feeling...

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.330
I’m still...

00:17:55.240 --> 00:18:00.180
Iruka-chan, how do you get such strength?

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:04.340
<i>Retasu, you need to have more faith in yourself.</i>

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:07.560
<i>Just do your best, it’s too early to give up now.</i>

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:11.400
<i>Though I’m afraid of the water now,</i>

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:15.860
<i>someday I’ll overcome my fears. I owe it all to Retasu-oneechan.</i>

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:20.350
I will... find the strength to do this!

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:32.200
This is, the same dream I had when I was drowning.

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:46.420
<i>Iruka-chan?</i>

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:48.350
<i>Who’s that?</i>

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:50.670
<i>R...Retasu-oneechan?</i>

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:51.810
<i>Yes.</i>

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:55.520
<i>You’re finally swimming,
really swimming!</i>

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:58.020
<i>Yes. Get ready, we’re going to fly.</i>

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:58.740
<i>Yes.</i>

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:06.520
Re... Retasu?

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:07.620
Her body...

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:13.200
What is this light?

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.050
Sunameri power?

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:21.370
These creatures live in the sea and
are weak under strong light.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.580
Alright, let’s go guys!

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:24.330
Yes.

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:24.980
Now!

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:27.940
Reborn... Mint ECHO!!

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:30.480
Reborn... PuddingRings INFERNO!!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.230
Reborn... Pomegran’ SPEAR!!

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:53.580
Reborn... Strawberry SURPRISE!!

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:11.020
Their plans were foiled again.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:14.230
Yes, the girls still have much to learn.

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:17.980
But about Mew Lettuce emanating that light...

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:21.770
We’ll discuss that when we return.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.470
Oh no! Bu-Ling-chan has fallen ill!

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:29.230
No way, you’re joking aren’t you?

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:31.250
If it’s true, there’s probably a nice proverb to describe it?

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.670
How about “The ogre with an iron club”
(overdoing things)?

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.690
“Reason with a cat” (poor judgement)?
“Preaching to a horse” (not listening)?

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:40.930
Those don’t describe the situation at all.
But seriously Bu-Ling-san is...

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:44.100
Next: “Memories of mother,
Oneechan is in trouble”

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:46.790
I got it! “Even a monkey can fall from its tree”

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:48.700
That’s not quite right either.

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:52.800
Didn’t I tell you Bu-Ling-san is seriously ill!!?
